{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781478842,"nonce":"4AG+pJU7tCAOveYnpktRS+qAie8=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABFdC09Q","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/270","origin":"github"},"title":"logger: record garmin water_temperature + nadir_depth in the main deployment bag","message":"The main deployment logger (`/**/logger:` in `bizzyboat.yaml` → the primary `bizzyboat` bag) records `/sound_speed` and `/tide_estimate`, but **not** the Garmin `water_temperature` / `nadir_depth` — those only land in the `sonar_logger` (`bizzyboat_sonar`) bag.\n\nSurfaced while validating Friday's (2026-06-12) Massabesic survey: the Garmin transducer **water temperature** is the independent cross-check on the AML-SVS sound speed (it confirmed the ~1505 m/s reading by showing ~26.8 °C → ~1501 m/s, a 0.26% match). But because it wasn't in the main bag, it had to be decoded from raw frames. These are tiny scalars and belong in the main deployment bag alongside `/sound_speed` so the primary bag is **self-contained** for the sound-speed / depth cross-check.\n\n## Change\nAdd to the `/**/logger:` record `topics` list (near `/sound_speed`):\n```\n- /bizzy/sensors/sidescan/garmin_sidescan/water_temperature\n- /bizzy/sensors/sidescan/garmin_sidescan/nadir_depth\n```\n\nFollow-up to #257 (added record+bridge to `sonar_logger` + `udp_bridge`, but not the main logger).\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}